@description REAPER Live - touch mixer and transport web interface
@version 0.5.0
@author Matthias Kronlachner
@provides
  reaper_mixer_live.html
@link https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix
@about
  # REAPER Live

  A touch-friendly mixer and transport for REAPER's built-in web server, meant
  for a phone or tablet propped next to you rather than for a desktop browser.

  - One strip per track plus the master: name, track colour, level meter and
    volume fader
  - **Padlocks for the things that can bite you.** MUTE/SOLO and the transport
    start **locked**; the faders start **unlocked**, since riding levels is
    the usual reason the tablet is there. Locked controls go dim and inert but
    stay visible, so mute, solo and play state can still be read at a glance
  - **Per-track fader locks.** Each strip header has its own padlock, for
    pinning the channels that must not move - a playback stem, a safety mic -
    while the rest stay live. The global fader lock overrides them
  - Faders drag **relatively**, so putting a finger down never jumps the level
    to where you touched. Double-tap resets a fader to 0 dB
  - Transport bar with go-to-start, stop, pause, play, record and repeat, plus
    the play position and time signature
  - Collapsible **markers panel** on the right: every marker and region with
    its time, the current ones highlighted; tap one to jump there (follows
    the transport lock)
  - Shows a banner and dims the mixer when REAPER stops answering, so a dead
    connection is obvious instead of looking like a frozen desk

  ## Setting it up

  ReaPack installs the page into `reaper_www_root/`, but REAPER still has to be
  told to serve it:

  1. Options -> Preferences -> Control/OSC/web
  2. Add (or edit) a **Web browser interface**
  3. Set a port, and choose `reaper_mixer_live.html` as the default web browser
     interface page
  4. Open `http://<computer-ip>:<port>/` on the phone or tablet

  Both devices need to be on the same network, and REAPER has to be running.
@changelog
  - Add a collapsible markers panel (Markers button in the transport bar):
    lists every marker and region, highlights the current ones, and jumps
    there on tap while the transport is unlocked
